# Trivy accepted risks for lab environment
# Cyber-Lab-v2 Phase 2

# AWS-0132: KMS CMK not required for lab environment.
# AES256 with AWS-managed keys provides sufficient protection at this scale.
# Production environments should use KMS CMK for key rotation control and audit trails.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0024: DynamoDB PITR not required for lock table.
# This table holds transient lock entries only. A lost lock is manually recoverable.
# Not a data store requiring point-in-time recovery.
AWS-0024

# AWS-0025: DynamoDB KMS CMK not required for lab.
# AWS-managed encryption is sufficient for a transient lock table at this scale.
AWS-0025

# AWS-0089: Access logging not enabled on logging and flow logs buckets.
# Enabling logging on the logging bucket creates a circular dependency.
# The flow logs bucket is itself a logging destination; recursive logging adds no value.
AWS-0089